// DAP (step 8.2): breakpoints by file and line. Set before the program
// runs, nothing is compiled yet: they are pending (verified false). The
// program is compiled one top-level statement at a time; after each one,
// before it runs, newtc installs the pending breakpoints that have code now
// and sends a "breakpoint" event (verified, at the line used: a line
// without code moves to the next statement, 12 -> 14). A new set for the
// file replaces the old one, also while stopped.
global Work(x)
begin
  local y := x + 1;
  y * 2;
end;

Print(Work(1));
Print(Work(2));
